**New evidence**
The 2022 record is mixed: there is real evidence of public disclosure, judicial scrutiny, and some independent corrections of accusations, but also repeated family-linked corruption cases and some appointments that cut both ways.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Detailed order on bail confirmation: No witness accused Shehbaz, Hamza of corruption: court","publisher":"Dawn","publication_date":"2022-06-14","url":"https://www.dawn.com/news/1694670","claim":"A special court said none of the prosecution witnesses accused Shehbaz Sharif or Hamza Shehbaz of bribery, kickbacks, or corrupt practices in the Rs16 billion money laundering case, and that cogent evidence was not yet available at the bail stage.","locator":"paragraphs 28-31 and 42-73","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous court reporting with direct quotations from the written order; the order itself is the underlying legal source.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target year and while Sharif was prime minister.","ruler_attribution":"This is a judicial assessment of allegations against Sharif and his son; it does not prove personal honesty, but it is directly relevant to the accused ruler-period record.","contrary_evidence":["The judge repeatedly cautioned that the bail observations were tentative and not a merits finding."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.6","7B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"PM Shehbaz tells court he refused salary as CM during Rs16bn money laundering hearing","publisher":"Dawn","publication_date":"2022-05-28","url":"https://www.dawn.com/news/1691904","claim":"Shehbaz Sharif testified in court that he refused salary and benefits when he was chief minister of Punjab and denied committing corruption.","locator":"paragraphs 41-46","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct report of a sworn court appearance and the ruler's own statement, though it is self-serving testimony.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target period.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Sharif as his own public testimony, but it is not independent proof of honesty.","contrary_evidence":["The statement was made in his own defense during a corruption case, so it is not independent corroboration."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"President Alvi appoints Ahad Cheema as adviser to the PM on establishment","publisher":"Dawn","publication_date":"2022-06-09","url":"https://www.dawn.com/news/1693934/president-alvi-appoints-ahad-cheema-as-adviser-to-the-pm-on-establishment","claim":"On the prime minister's advice, Ahad Cheema was appointed adviser to the PM on establishment; the report also notes his prior NAB arrest and inquiries linked to Ashiana-i-Iqbal and related cases.","locator":"lead paragraph and appointment notice","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct contemporaneous report of a formal PM-linked appointment and the appointee's corruption-case background.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Sharif's appointment power; the appointment cuts both ways because Cheema is a professional bureaucrat but also a controversial insider with pending case history.","contrary_evidence":["A career bureaucrat appointment can be read as competence-oriented, but the corruption baggage weakens the purity of that signal."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.9","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Accountability court grants PM Shehbaz permanent exemption from appearing in sugar scam case","publisher":"Dawn","publication_date":"2022-06-20","url":"https://www.dawn.com/news/1695803/accountability-court-grants-pm-shehbaz-permanent-exemption-from-appearing-in-sugar-scam-case","claim":"An accountability court granted Shehbaz Sharif permanent exemption in the Ramzan Sugar Mills case, while the NAB allegation was that he ordered a drain to benefit mills owned by his sons and caused loss to the exchequer; Sharif responded that the project served the area and that the provincial cabinet approved it.","locator":"lead and hearing summary","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct court reporting with the allegation and Sharif's answer on the record.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Sharif because the allegation concerns his own prior official action and his own explanation of it; the underlying guilt was not resolved in 2022.","contrary_evidence":["The court action concerns exemption and allegations, not a proven finding of self-dealing; Sharif also offered a public defense."],"lenses":["7B.3","7B.4","7B.6","7B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"PM’s son declared proclaimed offender","publisher":"Dawn","publication_date":"2022-07-16","url":"https://www.dawn.com/news/1699840","claim":"A special court declared Shehbaz Sharif's younger son Suleman a proclaimed offender in the money-laundering case and ordered his assets frozen, while the PM requested a one-time exemption from appearance.","locator":"paragraphs 38-46","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct contemporaneous court report with a concrete judicial order involving the ruler's immediate family.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"This is family-linked rather than a direct personal finding against Shehbaz; it matters because the chapter includes close-family benefit and tolerance, but the attribution to the PM is limited.","contrary_evidence":["A son's fugitive status is not proof that the PM personally directed the misconduct."],"lenses":["7B.4","7B.7","7B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"PM Shehbaz gets exemption from appearance in Ashiana case","publisher":"Dawn","publication_date":"2022-09-24","url":"https://www.dawn.com/news/1711703","claim":"An accountability court granted permanent exemption from personal appearance to Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif in the Ashiana-i-Iqbal Housing Scheme reference, where NAB alleged award of a no-bid contract and illegal gratification in the form of land.","locator":"lead paragraph and case summary","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct court reporting on a formal corruption case and the ruler's requested exemption.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Sharif because the allegations concern his own prior government action; the case remained contested, so this is not a merits finding.","contrary_evidence":["The article reports allegations rather than proof, and the exemption was procedural rather than a finding of guilt."],"lenses":["7B.3","7B.4","7B.6","7B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Lahore court acquits PM Shehbaz, son Hamza in Rs16bn money laundering case","publisher":"Dawn","publication_date":"2022-10-12","url":"https://www.dawn.com/news/1714663","claim":"A special court acquitted Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif and Hamza Shehbaz in the Rs16 billion money laundering case after the FIA told the court that no direct transaction had been made from benami accounts into their bank accounts.","locator":"lead paragraphs and hearing summary","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct contemporaneous court report on a dispositive judicial outcome.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly relevant to Sharif because it resolves a major corruption accusation against him and his son, although it does not affirmively prove virtue beyond the case outcome.","contrary_evidence":["An acquittal removes proof of this case, but it does not automatically establish broad personal integrity in all domains."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.6","7B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"FIA failed to link Shehbaz, Hamza to benami accounts: judge","publisher":"Dawn","publication_date":"2022-10-14","url":"https://www.dawn.com/news/1714961","claim":"The trial judge said the record was silent on any benefit to Shehbaz Sharif or Hamza from the alleged benami accounts, found no nexus between them and the accounts, and said there was no probability of conviction.","locator":"verdict summary in paragraphs 40-55","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct report of a detailed written judicial verdict.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly relevant to the ruler because the verdict addresses allegations against him and his son, but it remains case-specific rather than a full integrity audit.","contrary_evidence":["The verdict concerns one case and does not settle all corruption allegations about the family."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.6","7B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Not accused of any wrongdoing: Daily Mail apologises to PM Shehbaz for false corruption allegation","publisher":"Dawn","publication_date":"2022-12-08","url":"https://www.dawn.com/news/amp/1725318","claim":"The Daily Mail apologized to Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif, stating that he had never been accused by NAB of wrongdoing in relation to British public money or DFID grant aid and retracting the accusation that he stole aid money for earthquake victims.","locator":"lead and apology quotation in the article body","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"The piece reports an explicit correction and apology from the publication, though the article is a secondary report rather than the publisher's original notice.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective correction during 2022; relevant because it concerns a major corruption accusation against Sharif.","ruler_attribution":"This is not a ruler action, but it is an independent correction that materially weakens one prominent public corruption allegation against him.","contrary_evidence":["The apology concerns one historical allegation and does not resolve the separate domestic money-laundering cases."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.6","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"ECP releases data of assets owned by PM Shehbaz, Imran Khan, Zardari, and others","publisher":"Geo News","publication_date":"2022-06-15","url":"https://www.geo.tv/amp/422588-ecp-releases-data-of-assets-owned-by-pm-shehbaz-imran-khan-zardari-and-others","claim":"The ECP data released in 2022 showed Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif's assets at about Rs246 million, including London property, a small bank balance, liabilities, and a loan from his son Suleman.","locator":"article headline and opening paragraphs","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"The report is based on an official ECP asset disclosure, but the page is a media summary rather than the underlying filing.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Sharif's own disclosure and relevant to transparency, though it does not by itself prove clean governance or the absence of conflicts.","contrary_evidence":["Public asset disclosure is positive for transparency but not proof that no hidden conflicts or family entanglements existed."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.8","7B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I reviewed roughly 30 documents across Dawn, Geo, Gulf News, The News, Reuters syndications, Pakistani official notices, and court-reporting pieces. I kept the strongest ruler-specific items that tied directly to Sharif, his son, or his own court testimony, and I reused the earlier 5B professional-appointment evidence where it genuinely carried over.

I rejected repeated syndications of the same court story, broad corruption-index context with no personal nexus, and most political crossfire around Imran Khan because those items were either not about Sharif's own conduct or were only country-level context. I also treated several allegations as context-only when they lacked an independent finding or a clear link to Sharif's personal actions. Some prospective articles were blocked by cache misses when I tried to open them, so I leaned on the accessible court reports and the search-result text for those cases.

**Remaining gaps**
The record is good on 2022 legal scrutiny, acquittals, asset disclosure, and family-linked allegations, but weaker on proving a sustained pattern of personal deception or self-dealing beyond contested cases.

More search would help on:
1. Whether any 2022 appointments or contracts directly benefited Sharif family businesses or allies in a way that a court or audit specifically tied to him.
2. Whether his June-December 2022 transparency claims had any adverse findings in later audit, tax, or asset-disclosure records.
3. Whether the Ahad Cheema and other adviser appointments reflected merit, factional loyalty, or protection of insiders.
4. Whether the Daily Mail apology and the UK/NCA material can be tied to an official court finding rather than newspaper/editorial accounts.
5. Whether there are cleaner primary records on the Ramzan Sugar Mills and Ashiana references showing either exoneration or a sustained personal nexus.
